{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788468030-UVeXbHgLK7ZdDcPSUBY0","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `LocalPythonExecutor` now accepts an `additional_functions` parameter, matching upstream PR #1302 (the fix for issue #1301).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n- `src/smolagents/local_python_executor.py:1493` — added `additional_functions: dict[str, Callable] | None = None` as a third optional constructor parameter, stored as `self.additional_functions = additional_functions or {}`. Also added a class docstring documenting all three args.\n- `send_tools` (`src/smolagents/local_python_executor.py:1541`) now merges them: `{**tools, **BASE_PYTHON_TOOLS.copy(), **self.additional_functions}` — so your functions are combined with agent tools and base Python tools, and take precedence on a name collision. Since `CodeAgent` calls `send_tools` before every execution, the functions flow through both the agent path and direct executor use.\n- `tests/test_agents.py:1153` — added `test_local_python_executor_with_custom_functions` from the same PR as a regression test.\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```python\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a + b\n\nexecutor = LocalPythonExecutor(\n    additional_authorized_imports=[\"numpy\"],\n    max_print_outputs_length=10_000,\n    additional_functions={\"add\": add},\n)\nexecutor.send_tools({})\nexecutor(\"add(2, 3)\")  # -> 5\n```\n\n**Verification:**\n- Custom functions are callable in executed code, work after `send_variables`, and `print` output is still captured in logs separately from the return value; state persists across runs.\n- Security unchanged: `import os`, `open(...)`, `exec(...)`, and `__import__(...)` all still raise `InterpreterError`.\n- `tests/test_local_python_executor.py`: 335 passed, 2 skipped — the only 2 failures (`scipy`/`sklearn` import tests) are pre-existing in this environment because those packages aren't installed; they fail identically on the unmodified tree. `tests/test_agents.py::TestCodeAgent`: 13 passed, including the new test.\n\nOne note: passing a function named like a base tool (e.g. `\"print\"`) would override the sandboxed version, since additional functions are merged last — worth avoiding unless intentional.","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Parasail","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20044b2b-5320-4e51-b706-4ba170015569","uuid":"c47a8ba5-7b39-43d3-a866-b133e23a0f79","timestamp":"2026-09-03T20:40:44.645Z","request_id":"gen-1788468030-UVeXbHgLK7ZdDcPSUBY0"}
